# shellcheck shell=bash  # .envrc has no shebang (direnv evaluates it in bash); without this
# directive the shellcheck hook stops at SC2148. Declaring beats excluding: the file becomes
# CHECKED, and it is code that runs on every `cd` into the folder.
# direnv: on a `cd` into this repo, it enters flake.nix' devShells.default.
#
# WHAT THAT BUYS HERE: the devShell is what installs .git/hooks/pre-commit (git-hooks.nix'
# shellHook). Without the .envrc, "we have pre-commit" would depend on somebody running
# `nix develop` by hand, and in a fresh clone, in 2027, nobody is going to remember. With it, the
# first `cd` into the repo arms the hook on its own.
#
# It also brings statix/deadnix/nixfmt/nixd onto the PATH at the SAME versions the hooks use, so
# running them by hand gives the same result as the hook, with no dependence on the user's profile.
#
# `use flake` (and not `use nix`): it reads flake.nix' devShell, respecting flake.lock.
# nix-direnv (home/shell/cli.nix) caches the result, otherwise every `cd` would reevaluate the
# flake and the folder would take seconds to open.
#
# THE FIRST TIME, once per clone: `direnv allow`. It does NOT activate on its own on purpose,
# since an .envrc is code that runs when you enter the folder, so direnv demands explicit consent
# per file. That is why the .envrc is versioned but the permission is not.
# There is NO need for `eval "$shellHook"` here. I checked because it looked like there was: the
# nix-direnv direnvrc does not mention shellHook, which suggests it does not run. It does: what
# executes it is the rc generated by `nix print-dev-env`, whose LAST line is
# `eval "${shellHook:-}"` (checked in .direnv/flake-profile-*.rc). An extra eval here would run the
# hook twice for nothing.
#
# A DEBUGGING TRAP, which led me to the wrong conclusion first: the git-hooks shellHook is
# IDEMPOTENT through `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, not through the hook file. It only reinstalls if
# that symlink is missing or points at another store path ("compare before write", so it does not
# fight watchers like lorri). So deleting ONLY .git/hooks/pre-commit and reloading direnv does not
# bring it back: it looks like direnv is not working, and what is missing is deleting
# .pre-commit-config.yaml too.
use flake
